    affiliation: "Aurel Vlaicu University of Arad, Romania"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vbocan/ruin_framework"
abstract: >-
  RUIN (Rigor, Utility, Integrity, Necessity) is an experimental,
  language-model-assisted screen of computer science publications along four
  content-level dimensions: formalism proportionality, citation integrity,
  structural soundness, and artifact availability. The repository contains the
  framework specification, the ROMJIST dataset (421 records, 404 research
  papers, 2010–2025), a test–retest study whose protocol was fixed in advance,
  a retest of every capped paper, and scripts to reproduce the published tables
  and figures.
keywords:
  - research evaluation
  - scientometrics
  - formalism proportionality
  - reproducibility
  - large language models
  - content-based assessment
